    "body": "Raised P2 -> P1 on the suggestion of PR #911's high-tier review (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/911#pullrequestreview-5868416850): on a reduced-fidelity model the collision laws (shank / holder reach, rapids in stock, the turning rapid, bar-feed and holder scans) are not yet tightened and can read up to 0.01 mm too generous on a convex wall while an operation still posts. Other review notes for this issue: a stock copied from a coarse model loses its flag once that model is deleted; near the refusal edge the program sim can show a false gouge line instead of the named refusal; a project saved before #911 with an over-budget mesh loads as full fidelity with no re-check; \"re-import with a larger budget\" names a setting that does not exist yet.",
