    "body": "fix on issue/904-reduced-fidelity-laws (mkinney fork) · PR #1064 · pinned by camcraft-motion `turning_coarse`, camcraft-sim `coarse_collision` and `model_excess::the_envelope_laws_gouge_half_answers_to_the_tolerance_less_the_excess`, camcraft-app `coarse_laws`, `coarse_contain`, lib `rotary_law::tests` and `turning_rapids::tests::the_margin_generation_hands_the_law_shrinks_with_a_coarse_models_excess` · merges when reviewed\n\nPartial (`Refs #904`): turning, the rotary kinds and the multi-axis ball kinds are judged with tightened laws; the collision laws (reach, sweep, rapids, posed rapids, the turning margin, the rotary bands) read the excess; pins for point 6. Everything else this issue lists has its own issue, so this umbrella can close when the PR merges: #1052 (swarf), #1053 (cone and engrave rides, probe, cross drill, plasma), #1054 (facet budget setting), #1055 (metre-unit STEP), #1056 (flag gaps from #911's review, display tolerances). Also filed #1057: a matched drill is falsely convicted of a gouge on a model flagged above about 0.0105 mm - in the code #911 merged, not changed by this PR.",
